' Generated by daemon/install.ps1 (the tick) or daemon/tray-register.ps1 (a tray icon)
' from daemon/hidden-launcher.vbs.template - DO NOT EDIT.
' Runs a BotCorp pwsh script with no visible console (no flash).
'
' Why a VBS shim: a scheduled task running pwsh.exe directly flashes a console
' window every tick - `-WindowStyle Hidden` is honoured only AFTER conhost has
' drawn the window. wscript.exe is a GUI-subsystem host; WScript.Shell.Run(..., 0)
' starts pwsh with SW_HIDE before any window exists.
'
' pwsh is resolved at RUNTIME. A hardcoded versioned path (WindowsApps\...\7.x.y)
' breaks on EVERY PowerShell update and once silently killed a supervisor plus
' both of its monitors. Order: the runtime %LOCALAPPDATA% alias (correct under
' the default Password-logon task, which loads the profile), the alias path
' captured at install time (the S4U fallback runs WITHOUT the profile, so
' %LOCALAPPDATA% may point at the Default profile), then plain PATH lookup.
Dim sh, fso, pwsh, cmd
Set sh = CreateObject("WScript.Shell")
Set fso = CreateObject("Scripting.FileSystemObject")
' The runtime root is fixed at install time so the tick finds state/install.json
' (and pins the user profile from it) even when USERPROFILE is wrong (S4U).
sh.Environment("PROCESS")("BOTCORP_HOME") = "{{BOTCORP_HOME}}"
pwsh = sh.ExpandEnvironmentStrings("%LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\WindowsApps\pwsh.exe")
If Not fso.FileExists(pwsh) Then pwsh = "{{LOCALAPPDATA_PWSH}}"
If Not fso.FileExists(pwsh) Then pwsh = "pwsh.exe"
cmd = Chr(34) & pwsh & Chr(34) & " -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -WindowStyle Hidden -File " & Chr(34) & "{{TICK_SCRIPT}}" & Chr(34) & "{{SCRIPT_ARGS}}"
sh.Run cmd, 0, False
